WEBVTT

00:00:06.980 --> 00:00:15.700
Long, Hot Summer

00:00:06.980 --> 00:00:15.700
Performed by:
Iketeru Oniisan and Utano Oneesan

00:00:15.870 --> 00:00:23.080
♬ Where should we go this summer?
(It's summer!) ♬

00:00:23.080 --> 00:00:28.380
♬ The beach! The beach! The beach!
Let's go to the beach! ♬

00:00:28.380 --> 00:00:32.180
♬ It's summer, after all
(Summer, after all) ♬

00:00:32.180 --> 00:00:35.810
♬ Let's get stupid on the beach ♬

00:00:35.810 --> 00:00:41.230
♬ We can have a barbecue ♬

00:00:41.230 --> 00:00:45.320
♬ Pretend to have fun,
so nobody can tell ♬

00:00:45.320 --> 00:00:48.570
♬ That I spend my life ♬

00:00:48.570 --> 00:00:55.780
♬ Worried what other people think ♬

00:00:55.780 --> 00:00:57.620
♬ Ah-ah, this act doesn't suit me ♬

00:00:57.620 --> 00:00:59.200
♬ Oh, well, here it comes ♬

00:00:59.200 --> 00:01:01.250
♬ Better start acting dumber ♬

00:01:01.250 --> 00:01:06.630
♬ The long, hot summer ♬

00:01:13.930 --> 00:01:19.220
♬ The truth is, I want someone to say it ♬

00:01:19.220 --> 00:01:22.730
♬ "It's okay to spend the summer ♬

00:01:22.730 --> 00:01:27.020
♬ In a dark room with the A.C. on" ♬

00:01:27.020 --> 00:01:32.110
♬ "Just skip the darn music festivals" ♬

00:01:32.110 --> 00:01:39.410
♬ I lost sight of the mosquito,
and now I can't get to sleep ♬

00:01:39.410 --> 00:01:46.710
♬ When I got home,
the A.C. remote was gone ♬

00:01:46.710 --> 00:01:50.130
♬ My shirt's gross and sweaty ♬

00:01:50.130 --> 00:01:53.970
♬ And it's such a huge bummer ♬

00:01:53.970 --> 00:01:59.970
♬ The long, hot summer! ♬

00:02:10.190 --> 00:02:12.530
It was very cold.

00:02:12.530 --> 00:02:16.780
But now, it's so hot
that I miss that coldness.

00:02:16.780 --> 00:02:19.580
It's unusually hot this year.

00:02:21.290 --> 00:02:25.670
At any rate, wearing a costume like this
during summer is like hell, seriously.

00:02:25.670 --> 00:02:30.340
Yeah, but the A.C. is on inside
the studio, so it's not so bad, right?

00:02:30.340 --> 00:02:31.500
True.

00:02:32.670 --> 00:02:36.930
Hey! We'll have an outdoor
shoot today. So go outside!

00:02:39.930 --> 00:02:44.850
We'll shoot a music video for a new song
that will be used in the winter!

00:02:44.850 --> 00:02:48.100
The song title is "Subzero Spiral"!

00:02:48.100 --> 00:02:51.980
We got you winter clothes,
so change into them, okay?

00:02:51.980 --> 00:02:54.280
Let's give it our all!

00:04:20.360 --> 00:04:24.990
"LIFE LESSONS WITH URAMICHI ONIISAN"

00:04:25.030 --> 00:04:30.330
Episode 10: Subzero Spiral

00:04:46.140 --> 00:04:50.810
Okay, guys! Let's make another good MV!

00:04:56.270 --> 00:04:59.820
If we're shooting winter scenes,
wouldn't the indoor set be sufficient?

00:04:59.820 --> 00:05:04.160
No, no! Winter scenes
should have snow, right?

00:05:04.160 --> 00:05:08.870
Of course, we're going
to add snow using CG later.

00:05:08.870 --> 00:05:11.580
But atmosphere is important, right?

00:05:11.580 --> 00:05:17.170
When we have outdoor scenes, I think that
only using CG is taking the easy way out.

00:05:17.170 --> 00:05:22.130
Oh, yeah! We got a heater and a <i>kotatsu</i>
to create a more realistic atmosphere.

00:05:24.220 --> 00:05:29.100
Okay then, let's do the song
and check the flow of the video first.

00:05:29.100 --> 00:05:32.270
Sing in a winterly way, okay?
I'm counting on you!

00:05:32.270 --> 00:05:34.400
O-Okay.

00:05:34.400 --> 00:05:37.270
Aren't they gonna add the song later...?

00:05:43.070 --> 00:05:48.620
♬ Trodden-down snow is super dangerous ♬

00:05:46.870 --> 00:05:48.620
No, not like that!

00:05:48.620 --> 00:05:50.910
More winterly!

00:05:56.040 --> 00:06:01.630
♬ T-Trodden-down snow is super dangerous ♬

00:06:01.630 --> 00:06:07.640
♬ You fall flat just like that ♬

00:06:05.430 --> 00:06:07.640
Stop! Stop!

00:06:07.640 --> 00:06:10.680
I don't feel the coldness from you at all!

00:06:10.680 --> 00:06:16.350
Iketeru-<i>kun</i>! I asked you to express
a sense of winter with your singing!

00:06:16.350 --> 00:06:19.770
Right... I'm sorry.

00:06:19.770 --> 00:06:23.280
Winter... It's winter now.

00:06:23.280 --> 00:06:25.660
I live in winter right now.

00:06:25.660 --> 00:06:27.740
It's winter now. It's winter now.

00:06:27.740 --> 00:06:32.870
It's winter now. It's winter now.
It's winter now...

00:06:32.870 --> 00:06:34.000
Iketeru Oniisan!

00:06:34.000 --> 00:06:38.340
Your potential is incredible, but pushing
yourself in this heat is dangerous!

00:06:38.340 --> 00:06:41.090
You're right, I can't do it.

00:06:41.090 --> 00:06:43.420
Yeah, of course.

00:06:43.420 --> 00:06:46.590
Uramichi Oniisan.

00:06:46.590 --> 00:06:51.060
Right! That's good, Iketeru-<i>kun</i>!
It's starting to look winterly!

00:06:51.060 --> 00:06:53.930
Uramichi-<i>san</i>. What's that?

00:06:53.930 --> 00:06:56.020
Hm? Which one?

00:06:56.020 --> 00:07:01.070
That thing you're holding...
Um, that s-snow... Snowma...? S-S-S-Sno--

00:07:01.070 --> 00:07:03.320
No matter how you look at it,
it's a snowman.

00:07:03.320 --> 00:07:07.700
Right after I got here, they gave me
this and asked me to draw its face.

00:07:07.700 --> 00:07:09.120
I see.

00:07:09.120 --> 00:07:13.040
What about you? Why are you holding
a banana so dearly like that?

00:07:13.040 --> 00:07:14.870
Oh, this?

00:07:14.870 --> 00:07:16.540
Ennoshita-<i>san </i>said earlier,

00:07:16.540 --> 00:07:18.250
"Please eat this,"

00:07:18.250 --> 00:07:20.540
and gave it to me.

00:07:20.540 --> 00:07:22.000
I see.

00:07:22.000 --> 00:07:23.510
Why don't you hurry up and eat it?

00:07:23.510 --> 00:07:27.180
Well, I wanted to
cherish it a little longer.

00:07:27.180 --> 00:07:28.390
It's gonna go bad.

00:07:28.390 --> 00:07:30.390
Usao-<i>san</i>!

00:07:30.390 --> 00:07:32.220
Y-Yes?!

00:07:32.220 --> 00:07:35.060
Did you eat that banana?

00:07:35.060 --> 00:07:39.350
Err... Not yet. I thought I'd take
my time and enjoy it thoroughly.

00:07:39.350 --> 00:07:41.770
Oh... I see.

00:07:41.770 --> 00:07:44.940
We'll be using the skin,
so please keep it with you.

00:07:44.940 --> 00:07:46.190
What?

00:07:46.190 --> 00:07:49.910
There are scenes in the MV
where you slip and fall on snow.

00:07:49.910 --> 00:07:51.990
But we couldn't find anything
that would help you slip,

00:07:51.990 --> 00:07:54.870
so we decided to use a banana.

00:07:54.870 --> 00:07:58.000
So please don't throw it away
and keep it handy.

00:07:59.500 --> 00:08:01.420
Oh...

00:08:01.420 --> 00:08:03.210
Okay.

00:08:03.210 --> 00:08:05.960
Using a banana... In this day and age...?

00:08:05.960 --> 00:08:07.300
Oof.

00:08:07.300 --> 00:08:10.140
You guys are being sloppy.

00:08:10.140 --> 00:08:12.220
I'm not evil, you know.

00:08:12.220 --> 00:08:18.100
The kotatsu and heater here
don't have the power turned on!

00:08:18.100 --> 00:08:19.520
They'd better not.

00:08:19.520 --> 00:08:20.600
What?

00:08:20.600 --> 00:08:22.360
Nothing.

00:08:25.610 --> 00:08:31.240
The part "The air in the room froze
white like a cloudy midwinter sky"

00:08:31.240 --> 00:08:33.700
means extraordinary coldness.

00:08:33.700 --> 00:08:37.700
I want you to express
that extreme coldness!

00:08:37.700 --> 00:08:42.580
You know... To put it simply...
it's really cold.

00:08:42.580 --> 00:08:45.670
How should I put it?
It's extremely cold, you know!

00:08:43.340 --> 00:08:46.590
Is this <i>kotatsu </i>really not powered on?

00:08:45.670 --> 00:08:51.050
How should I put it?
It's extreme coldness.

00:08:46.590 --> 00:08:48.420
It's steamy inside, isn't it?

00:08:51.050 --> 00:08:55.560
To put it simply,
it's really, seriously cold!

00:08:55.560 --> 00:08:56.850
Get it?

00:08:56.850 --> 00:08:58.770
Right.

00:08:58.770 --> 00:08:59.980
Hm?

00:09:09.440 --> 00:09:13.320
Listen guys. It's winter right now.

00:09:09.520 --> 00:09:13.400
Because it's summer, drink soda!
Refreshing soda

00:09:09.520 --> 00:09:13.400
Because it's summer, drink soda!
Refreshing soda

00:09:13.740 --> 00:09:17.410
It's really cold. Do you get it?

00:09:17.410 --> 00:09:20.040
See? There are some snow flurries.

00:09:20.040 --> 00:09:21.830
What?

00:09:21.830 --> 00:09:24.170
There aren't any.

00:09:24.170 --> 00:09:26.210
See it with your inner eye.

00:09:26.210 --> 00:09:29.050
Uramichi-<i>kun</i>. What do you like
to drink on days like this?

00:09:29.050 --> 00:09:31.300
Ice-cold beer.

00:09:30.000 --> 00:09:32.760
"Draft Beer"

00:09:31.300 --> 00:09:34.050
No! Warm <i>oshiruko</i>, right?!

00:09:32.630 --> 00:09:37.800
"Oshirukko with 
Azuki Beans"

00:09:34.050 --> 00:09:38.060
The moisture inside my mouth is
evaporating just thinking about it.

00:09:38.060 --> 00:09:40.430
Okay, Utano-<i>chan</i>.
What would you like to drink?

00:09:40.430 --> 00:09:42.560
Ice-cold beer.

00:09:42.560 --> 00:09:45.270
Jeez... How about you, Iketeru-<i>kun</i>?!

00:09:45.270 --> 00:09:46.860
Cream soda...

00:09:46.860 --> 00:09:47.980
How cute...

00:09:47.980 --> 00:09:50.690
Cute, but wrong answer!

00:09:50.690 --> 00:09:52.990
Fine! Let's move on to the next scene!

00:09:52.990 --> 00:09:55.280
The scene where you're having a bonfire!

00:09:53.780 --> 00:09:56.120
Hey... Hey...!

00:09:55.280 --> 00:10:00.040
Now! Hurry up and get the bonfire ready!

00:09:56.120 --> 00:10:00.040
Hey!

00:10:00.040 --> 00:10:01.120
Hm?

00:10:02.540 --> 00:10:03.830
Hey...

00:10:09.000 --> 00:10:11.550
Wait, Kumatani! Restrain your--

00:10:11.550 --> 00:10:14.510
Ow... Ow... Ow...

00:10:14.510 --> 00:10:16.340
Whoa! Your body's trunk is so weak!

00:10:22.270 --> 00:10:23.600
Derekida-<i>san</i>.

00:10:23.600 --> 00:10:25.520
Y-Yes?

00:10:25.520 --> 00:10:30.400
I just can't figure out how Kumao
should perform this song.

00:10:30.400 --> 00:10:32.860
Please show me how, Derekida-<i>san</i>.

00:10:32.860 --> 00:10:37.070
I'd be able to understand it
if I saw it with my own eyes.

00:10:37.070 --> 00:10:39.450
What? What?

00:10:39.450 --> 00:10:41.330
What? Kumatani-<i>kun</i>?

00:10:41.330 --> 00:10:44.620
Hey! What're you-- Stop it!

00:10:44.620 --> 00:10:46.790
K-Kumatani...

00:10:46.790 --> 00:10:47.880
What?!

00:10:49.500 --> 00:10:53.420
Hot! What's this?! How does this work?!

00:10:53.420 --> 00:10:56.550
Hey! I can't take this off!

00:10:56.550 --> 00:10:57.640
What?!

00:10:57.640 --> 00:10:59.180
<i>Kuma!</i>

00:11:05.310 --> 00:11:06.900
The director collapsed!

00:11:06.900 --> 00:11:08.730
We're taking a break!

00:11:08.730 --> 00:11:11.360
We're going back to the studio for now!

00:11:12.780 --> 00:11:17.740
At his previous job, he threw a punch
at his abusive boss and got fired...

00:11:17.740 --> 00:11:18.870
What?

00:11:18.870 --> 00:11:23.040
He had really good business performance
and was on the fast track.

00:11:23.040 --> 00:11:24.700
I didn't know...

00:11:24.700 --> 00:11:25.960
And it happened twice.

00:11:25.960 --> 00:11:30.000
Twice?! Is he good or bad at his job?

00:11:30.000 --> 00:11:32.670
Uramichi Oniisan...

00:11:37.050 --> 00:11:41.640
After yesterday's outdoor shoot, I really
appreciate how cool inside the studio is.

00:11:41.640 --> 00:11:46.520
It's like we went on a trip in order
to reconfirm how nice our own home is.

00:11:48.480 --> 00:11:50.310
What? What was that?

00:11:50.310 --> 00:11:54.190
Err... Never mind. After saying that,
I thought it sounded kind of off, too.

00:11:54.190 --> 00:11:56.320
What was that? What did you mean?

00:11:56.320 --> 00:11:58.910
What? Wh-What did you mean?

00:11:57.570 --> 00:12:01.490
Why is he so curious
about this? Just let it go!

00:11:58.910 --> 00:12:01.490
What was that? A trip?
What did you mean?

00:12:01.490 --> 00:12:04.830
At any rate, yesterday was
really rough, wasn't it?

00:12:04.830 --> 00:12:07.370
I got tanned even though I used sunscreen.

00:12:07.370 --> 00:12:11.750
If Kumatani didn't practically
force them to give us a break,

00:12:11.750 --> 00:12:14.380
there might've been some casualties.

00:12:16.630 --> 00:12:18.630
Hey, guys!

00:12:18.630 --> 00:12:20.140
Hello.

00:12:20.140 --> 00:12:22.970
I'm looking forward to
another great performance!

00:12:25.680 --> 00:12:27.890
Ah... K-Kumatani-<i>kun</i>.

00:12:27.890 --> 00:12:30.480
I mean, Kumatani-<i>chan</i>.

00:12:30.480 --> 00:12:31.310
Huh?

00:12:31.310 --> 00:12:33.980
I mean... Kumatani-<i>san</i>.

00:12:33.980 --> 00:12:37.490
H-How is the A.C. working for you?

00:12:37.490 --> 00:12:40.740
Please turn it down by one degree or so.

00:12:40.740 --> 00:12:44.410
Hey, ADs! Make sure
the A.C. is working well!

00:12:44.410 --> 00:12:46.120
Okay!

00:12:46.120 --> 00:12:48.580
He's hard only on us, isn't he?

00:12:48.580 --> 00:12:51.830
I wish he had stayed collapsed.

00:12:51.830 --> 00:12:56.760
Hey, you two! What're you whispering
about?! You seem like you're having fun!

00:12:56.760 --> 00:12:57.880
Oh, crap! He's coming this way!

00:12:57.880 --> 00:12:59.470
Run!

00:12:59.470 --> 00:13:01.590
L-Let me join you!

00:13:01.590 --> 00:13:06.180
What could you have done?
Anyone would have hit the guy.

00:13:06.180 --> 00:13:11.310
She's right. With the heat like that,
you can't think straight, either.

00:13:11.310 --> 00:13:14.400
You weren't really at fault, Kumatani.

00:13:16.940 --> 00:13:20.490
When will the punishment
for Kumatani-<i>san </i>be decided?

00:13:21.820 --> 00:13:27.040
We'll testify as much as possible
so that you can at least keep your job.

00:13:27.040 --> 00:13:29.040
Yep, yep.

00:13:29.040 --> 00:13:32.500
Well, I didn't throw a punch this time.

00:13:34.790 --> 00:13:39.010
Whoa... With this many people,
no reaction to what I said?

00:13:39.010 --> 00:13:41.510
It's quite hard to find a new job,

00:13:41.510 --> 00:13:45.260
so I wouldn't do anything
reckless for something like this.

00:13:45.260 --> 00:13:48.930
Oh, speaking of which,
why did you punch your boss

00:13:48.930 --> 00:13:51.140
at the company you got fired from?

00:13:51.140 --> 00:13:55.940
That... was because I kind of got ticked.

00:13:55.940 --> 00:13:57.730
That's the reason?

00:14:00.940 --> 00:14:02.860
We're about to start shooting.

00:14:02.860 --> 00:14:04.780
Please get ready.

00:14:04.780 --> 00:14:06.240
Okay.

00:14:06.780 --> 00:14:08.990
"TOGETHER WITH MAMAN"

00:14:07.830 --> 00:14:11.500
Hello, kids! How are you?!

00:14:11.500 --> 00:14:14.920
Let's begin the ABC Exercise--

00:14:14.920 --> 00:14:16.960
Uramichi Oniisan!

00:14:16.960 --> 00:14:19.550
Hm? What's up?

00:14:19.550 --> 00:14:21.800
What's "harassment"?!

00:14:23.720 --> 00:14:28.100
Well... I don't exactly
know what it is, either.

00:14:28.100 --> 00:14:31.350
You don't know even
though you're an adult?

00:14:31.350 --> 00:14:35.900
The meaning of a word can take
on a life of its own as a concept

00:14:35.900 --> 00:14:38.480
and start changing, so...

00:14:38.480 --> 00:14:40.400
Is the word "harassment" like that, too?

00:14:40.400 --> 00:14:44.150
As for "harassment," it hasn't
just taken on a life of its own.

00:14:44.150 --> 00:14:46.780
I'd say it's gotten out of control.

00:14:46.860 --> 00:14:48.570
"Harassment"

00:14:48.950 --> 00:14:50.740
So "harassment" is out of control?!

00:14:50.740 --> 00:14:53.080
"Harassment" is scary.

00:14:53.080 --> 00:14:54.750
It was named by adults, who got confused

00:14:54.750 --> 00:14:56.920
because they couldn't
follow the principle that

00:14:56.920 --> 00:15:00.590
"you shouldn't do things that
you don't want others to do to you,"

00:15:00.590 --> 00:15:05.510
which is a simple rule
that you learn at a nursery school.

00:15:05.510 --> 00:15:08.930
Why do they name things
when they get confused?

00:15:08.930 --> 00:15:13.020
Adults are afraid of transparent things
because they can't see them.

00:15:13.020 --> 00:15:17.690
So, they put a color called "name" on it
to make it visible as a first step.

00:15:13.100 --> 00:15:22.440
Harassment

00:15:17.690 --> 00:15:21.900
But in return, the word becomes
stronger because it now has a name,

00:15:21.900 --> 00:15:25.030
so adults, who're slow,
can no longer catch it.

00:15:25.030 --> 00:15:27.070
Are adults stupid?

00:15:27.070 --> 00:15:31.410
If they weren't, "harassment"
would've long become extinct.

00:15:31.410 --> 00:15:32.870
Like dinosaurs?

00:15:32.870 --> 00:15:35.080
Like dinosaurs.

00:15:35.080 --> 00:15:39.210
The truth is, no matter how stupid the
person is, you shouldn't punch them.

00:15:39.210 --> 00:15:41.920
But some idiots won't get it
unless they're punched.

00:15:41.920 --> 00:15:44.550
Though it's a confusing society,

00:15:44.550 --> 00:15:50.180
you kids will be thrown into such
a world when you become adults.

00:16:05.690 --> 00:16:07.570
Please bring me home with you

00:16:50.820 --> 00:16:54.410
Is it okay to punch an idiot who wouldn't
get it unless they're punched?

00:16:54.410 --> 00:16:59.040
Hurting someone also
means hurting yourself.

00:16:59.040 --> 00:17:00.710
As long as you know that,

00:17:00.710 --> 00:17:05.210
I think you'll be able to decide
on your own when the time comes.

00:17:09.880 --> 00:17:12.220
Ah! I fell asleep!

00:17:12.220 --> 00:17:13.850
Kumatani! Are we going out yet?

00:17:13.850 --> 00:17:16.310
Shut up. Stay asleep
the rest of your life.

00:17:16.310 --> 00:17:20.140
Th-That's not nice. That's verbal abuse.
It's power harassment.

00:17:20.140 --> 00:17:22.560
You mean, "moral harassment."

00:17:32.610 --> 00:17:34.240
Hello.

00:17:34.240 --> 00:17:35.740
Hey.

00:17:40.910 --> 00:17:43.380
May I have one?

00:17:43.380 --> 00:17:45.500
I thought you quit.

00:17:45.500 --> 00:17:47.170
Just for today.

00:17:47.170 --> 00:17:48.760
Just one.

00:17:56.550 --> 00:18:01.890
I don't remember why I punched him at all.

00:18:01.890 --> 00:18:04.650
But...

00:18:04.650 --> 00:18:07.570
...one thing I remember is that
the cigarette after slamming

00:18:07.570 --> 00:18:11.740
my letter of resignation on his desk,
was the best I'd ever tasted in my life.

00:18:17.330 --> 00:18:18.620
I see.

00:19:54.880 --> 00:19:56.420
So, what do you think?

00:19:56.420 --> 00:19:59.510
This is good! It's the best!

00:19:59.510 --> 00:20:01.810
It looks wonderful!

00:20:01.810 --> 00:20:03.350
I know, right?

00:20:03.350 --> 00:20:05.890
Oh, Uramichi-<i>kun</i>! Good timing.

00:20:05.890 --> 00:20:07.810
Check this out.

00:20:07.810 --> 00:20:10.060
These facial expressions here
are captured very well.

00:20:10.060 --> 00:20:11.820
Yeah, they are.

00:20:11.820 --> 00:20:13.610
What're you guys watching?

00:20:13.610 --> 00:20:15.780
Ah! Utano-<i>chan</i>!

00:20:15.780 --> 00:20:18.410
You know, this is a masterpiece.

00:20:18.410 --> 00:20:19.450
What is it?

00:20:19.450 --> 00:20:22.910
The "Subzero Spiral" music video!

00:20:19.530 --> 00:20:22.990
"Subzero Spiral"

00:20:23.870 --> 00:20:26.450
The editing team got in the groove,

00:20:26.450 --> 00:20:29.170
so it's pretty much done.
Take a look. It's the best.

00:20:29.170 --> 00:20:34.000
What? We shot it the day before
yesterday. Isn't this too quick?

00:20:34.000 --> 00:20:40.220
Well, the "Long, Hot Summer"
MV was... um... a little... you know...

00:20:40.220 --> 00:20:42.930
Hm? Oh, that.

00:20:42.930 --> 00:20:45.100
That was super good, too.

00:20:45.100 --> 00:20:48.180
But this one is even better!

00:20:48.180 --> 00:20:52.610
Really! Our hard work outdoors
in the heat was worthwhile!

00:20:52.610 --> 00:20:53.310
See?!

00:20:53.310 --> 00:20:53.820
Hm?

